cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this design, please cite it as below."
title: "Yeah Hand (formerly Rebelia): an open source tendon-driven robotic and prosthetic hand"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lumare"
    given-names: "Vittorio"
    affiliation: "RobotGarage"
    email: "vittorio.lumare@robotgarage.org"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
abstract: >-
  Open source anthropomorphic hand, fully 3D-printable, usable as a robotic end
  effector and as an active prosthetic hand. Five serial bus servomotors housed
  in the hand skeleton drive the fingers through antagonistic flexion and extension
  tendons wound on one spool per actuator; ring and little fingers are coupled
  through a sliding tendon loop; the ESP32-based firmware provides load-based
  tendon calibration, force-limited grasps, grasp presets and two-channel FFT-based EMG control.
repository-code: "https://github.com/opsobot/rebelia"
url: "https://www.robotgarage.org"
license: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-03-03"
keywords:
  - open source hardware
  - robotic hand
  - prosthetic hand
  - tendon-driven
  - underactuated
  - gripper
  - 3D printing
  - ESP32
